## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design privacy-preserving cross-tenant scoring with hardware attestation, threshold cryptography, and a verifiable ledger. Evaluates threat modeling, replay protection, and isolation guarantees.

## Key Concepts

- Hardware attestation (TEE/TPM) to validate shares
- Threshold cryptography for secure aggregation
- Tamper-evident ledger using Merkle trees
- Zero-knowledge proofs to prove correctness without exposing data
- Multi-tenant isolation and robust replay protection

